From 06834217cbbf29297880ebd5016e54c1d4864fb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 02:44:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 57/98] pco: don't back-propagate pixout into source-encoded
 dests

Fixes 2280bf4 ("pco: back-propagate pixel output writes again").

The data register of e.g. a texture sample is encoded as a source
(dest_intrn_map), so the legalizer treats a pixout dest there like a
source and inserts a mov *from* the pixout register before the sample:
the sampled value never reached the output. Hit by internal transfer
shaders, e.g. the depth readback in
dEQP-VK.fragment_operations.early_fragment.samplemask_no_early_fragment_tests_depth_samples_{2,4}.

Only back-propagate pixout into instructions whose dest is a real
destination. Both tests pass again; a 5062-case CTS selection (glsl
operators/builtins, compute, fragment_operations, discard/demote,
SPIR-V integer ops) now matches the d253e35 baseline exactly.
---
 src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c b/src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c
index fac4293..a4d9822 100644
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c
@@ -263,6 +263,12 @@ static inline bool try_back_prop_instr(struct pco_use *uses, pco_instr *instr)
 
    if (pco_ref_is_reg(*pdest_from) &&
        pco_ref_get_reg_class(*pdest_from) == PCO_REG_CLASS_PIXOUT) {
+      /* A dest encoded as a source register (e.g. the data register of a
+       * sample) is legalized like a source, which would read the pixout reg
+       * before the write instead of moving the result into it after.
+       */
+      if (pco_op_info[instr->op].dest_intrn_map[0])
+         return false;
 
       bool has_isp_fb = false;
 
